---
source: crates/web/src/tests.rs
expression: "readable(&f, chat)"
---
<section id="chat">
<h2>Chat with the reviewer</h2>
<p>Ask the agent that did run 1 about its review. Paste this into a terminal:</p>
<div class="copyable">
<pre id="chat-command">
<code>$EXE chat 1 --config '/config/sanic review.toml' --data-dir $DATA</code>
</pre>
<button type="button" data-copy="#chat-command">Copy</button>
</div>
<p class="dim">It checks the review's worktree out again, at the path the review used, and removes it when the chat ends. The agent keeps the review's limits: read-only tools and no GitHub token. Add <code>--allow-edits</code> to let it edit that copy of the worktree.</p>
<details>
<summary>Or run claude yourself</summary>
<p>This needs the worktree, which <code>$EXE chat --print-command 1 --config '/config/sanic review.toml' --data-dir $DATA</code> checks out and prints this line for. Remove the worktree afterwards with <code>$EXE chat --cleanup 1 --config '/config/sanic review.toml' --data-dir $DATA</code>.</p>
<div class="copyable">
<pre id="claude-command">
<code>cd $DATA/worktrees/1 &amp;&amp; env -u GITHUB_TOKEN -u GH_TOKEN -u GITHUB_ENTERPRISE_TOKEN -u GH_ENTERPRISE_TOKEN '/opt/my claude' --resume sess-7 --restricted --strict-mcp-config --tools Read,Grep,Glob --allowedTools Read,Grep,Glob --add-dir $DATA/runs/1 --add-dir /skills/review</code>
</pre>
<button type="button" data-copy="#claude-command">Copy</button>
</div>
</details>
</section>
